  "findings": "Compared photographed leaf tufts, rhizomes and blades with current three-size pilots and all 36 variants. The New Zealand October views are southern spring structure references; the extracted plant photograph exposes the basal tillers. Reduced blade count, narrowed rachis capsules and restored taller curved blades after the first batch looked like a solid short tuft. Current 0.20-0.42 m blades form open upright or spreading vegetative tufts without summer seed panicles. The 25 mm cells visibly exaggerate millimetre-wide Poa blades; this is an intentional coarse voxel representation and cannot capture boat-shaped tips. Accepted for spring ground-cover review, pending user seed endorsement.",
